    "type": "text",
    "topic": "epilepsy diagnosis",
    "problem": "Shorter duration of slow wave sleep is related to symptoms of depression in patients with epilepsy Slow wave sleep duration and spectral abnormalities are related to both epilepsy and depression, but it is unclear how depressive symptoms in patients with epilepsy are affected by slow wave sleep duration and clinical factors, and how the spectral characteristics of slow wave sleep reflect a\u2026",
    "solution": "Depressive symptoms were documented with the Beck Depression Inventory (BDI). At least mild depressive symptoms (BDI>9) were found among 23 patients with focal epilepsy, 5 patients with generalised epilepsy, and 6 patients who had no epilepsy diagnosis. Slow wave sleep duration was shorter for patients with at least mild depressive symptoms (p=.004), independently from epilepsy diagnosis,\u2026",
    "source": "arxiv"
  }
